# .sandcastle/.env — values the Engine's `resolveEnv` merges into EVERY sandbox.
# Copy to .sandcastle/.env and fill in. This file is gitignored (see .gitignore);
# it never ships the Factory's own values.
#
#   cp .sandcastle/.env.example .sandcastle/.env
#
# ⚠ ONLY the host-CLI token belongs here. The provider LLM tokens
# (ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN / CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN) MUST NOT — resolveEnv would leak
# them into every sandbox and claude-code would send the wrong token to the wrong
# base URL (401). Put those in .sandcastle/.env.secrets (or export them in your
# shell). main.ts throws at startup if .env declares any active provider's tokenKey.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host-CLI token (issue #17)
#
# The planner/implementer prompts run `gh` / `glab` INSIDE the agent sandbox, and that
# sandbox must have the CLI authed. resolveEnv flows THIS file into every sandbox, so
# the conventionally-named token placed here auths the in-sandbox CLI with NO main.ts
# patch. Set the ONE var matching your `gitHost` (config.ts):
#
#   gitHost: 'glab'  →  GITLAB_TOKEN      (default)
#   gitHost: 'gh'    →  GH_TOKEN
#   gitHost: 'local' →  (none — no host CLI, no token required)
#
# Precedence: a token exported in your shell (~/.bashrc) WINS over a value here, and
# resolveEnv picks up env vars too — so exporting it once means this file is optional.
# main.ts validates the token is present at startup (naming this file) and never logs
# its value. Obtain it with the host CLI after `gh auth login` / `glab auth login`:
#
#   gh auth login    && gh auth token       # → GH_TOKEN      (gitHost: 'gh')
#   glab auth login  && glab auth token     # → GITLAB_TOKEN  (gitHost: 'glab')

# Default host (gitHost: 'glab') — uncomment for a GitLab consumer.
# GITLAB_TOKEN=

# GitHub consumer (gitHost: 'gh') — uncomment instead of the line above.
# GH_TOKEN=
